# SMILE 7.0.0 Release Notes

Welcome to **SMILE 7.0.0**! This major release unifies high-performance JVM machine learning with the next generation of agentic data science. Version 7.0.0 introduces autonomous desktop automation, multi-agent orchestration, high-throughput LLM serving with batched Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) speculative decoding, native Kotlin and Scala 3 notebook kernels, an extensive productivity and research skills suite, time series forecasting (ARIMA/ARMA), and comprehensive stability and security hardening across Studio and the Agent harness.

---

## ✨ New Features

### 🤖 AI Agents & Desktop Automation
- **🖥️ Desktop Operator Agent (`@chuck`)**:
  - Introduced Chuck, a specialized desktop automation agent capable of interacting directly with GUI applications via screenshot analysis, mouse navigation, and keyboard control.
  - Safe desktop automation pipeline with coordinate mapping, interactive user confirmation, and automatic session bounds.
- **👔 Chief of Staff Agent (`@frank`)**:
  - Added Frank to coordinate multi-agent teams, synthesize status reports across active agents, track project priorities, and lead cross-agent briefings.
- **Dynamic Agent Catalog**:
  - Studio now discovers and loads agent personas dynamically from configuration specifications, with clean peer-to-peer delegation and request queuing.

### ⚡ High-Performance LLM Serving & Speculative Decoding
- **Batched Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) Speculative Decoding**:
  - Implemented high-throughput batched MTP speculative decoding with persistent per-request draft histories, enabled by default in `smile.serve`.
  - Accelerated generation with fused DeltaNet window operations, eager FlashInfer attention, and CUDA graph verification for low-latency token generation.
- **SHAP Explanations in Model Serving**:
  - Native SHAP explanation payloads in REST inference responses with clean 3-decimal formatting and zero overhead when unrequested.
- **Dynamic Model Loading & Control APIs**:
  - Dynamically load and unload models on the fly via `POST /api/v1/models/load`.
  - Added real-time telemetry, model control, and health endpoints (`/smile/{id}`, `/onnx/{id}`, and `/q/health`).
  - Native Prometheus metrics scraping integration.
  - Support for ONNX Runtime 1.30, ONNX Runtime GenAI models (including Phi-4 mini), LibTorch 2.14.1, and automatic KV-cache precision selection (`auto`).
- **Centralized Prometheus metrics API**:
  - **`GET /q/metrics`:** Single scrape target formatted according to standard Prometheus text specifications.
  - **Multidimensional Labeling:** Every time-series metric carries a `model_id` label, allowing unified visualization dashboards (e.g., Grafana) with dynamic multi-tenant filtering.
  - **Microsecond Precision:** Latency observations, throughput gauges, and cache counters are recorded with sub-millisecond fidelity via Micrometer.
  - **Non-blocking Execution:** Metric tracking uses atomic primitives and lightweight histograms without introducing latency penalties to inference pipelines.

### 📚 Expanded Skills Suite
- **Comprehensive Document Processing**:
  - **Excel (`excel-processing`)**: Read, analyze, create, and format spreadsheets (`.xlsx`, `.csv`) with support for formulas, styles, and embedded charts.
  - **Word (`word-processing`)**: Parse, edit, and generate Microsoft Word documents (`.docx`) with precise layout and typography control.
  - **PDF (`pdf-processing`)**: Extract, analyze, and render publication-quality PDF reports and slide decks.
- **Research & Development Skills**:
  - **Deep Research (`research`)**: Multi-source web search and structured synthesis for market research and competitive analysis.
  - **Weekly Briefing (`weekly-briefing`)**: Automated status roll-ups and progress tracking across all agent session logs.
  - **Scientific Posters (`posters`)**: Design and generate conference posters and presentation materials.
  - **Git Commit (`git-commit`)**: Intelligent, conventional commit generation from working directory diffs.
  - **Skill Creator (`skill-creator`)**: Interactive creation, evaluation, and optimization of custom agent skills.

### 📓 Interactive Notebooks & Polyglot Data Science
- **🚀 Native Kotlin Scripting Kernel**:
  - Interactive Kotlin notebooks (`.kts`) powered by the Kotlin Custom Scripting Host API with full access to SMILE algorithms.
- **⚡ AST-Aware Scala 3 Evaluation**:
  - `ScalaKernel` now parses code using the Scala 3 compiler to evaluate complete top-level classes, multi-line blocks, and closures without timeouts or truncation.
- **Interactive Welcome & Release Notes**:
  - Replaced the blank starting file with an interactive `Welcome` tutorial and dedicated `Release Notes` viewer.

### 📈 Machine Learning, Analytics & Core Engine
- **Time Series Analysis (ARIMA & ARMA)**:
  - Added `smile.timeseries.ARIMA` supporting arbitrary differencing, stationary transformation, and recursive multi-step forecasting.
  - Added model selection diagnostics: Gaussian log-likelihood, AIC, BIC, RSS, and coefficient $t$-test tables.
  - Added pure MA fitting via Hannan-Rissanen stage-2 least squares in `smile.timeseries.ARMA`.
- **Unit-Hypercube Hyperparameter Optimization (HPO)**:
  - Added `smile.hpo.ParameterSpace` supporting continuous, integer, and discrete search spaces normalized into a unit hypercube $[0, 1]^d$, with uniform candidate sampling and elite local perturbations.
- **Local Outlier Factor (LOF) Anomaly Detection**:
  - Density-based anomaly detection via `smile.anomaly.LOF<T>` across arbitrary metric spaces.
- **Tree Ensemble Feature Selection**:
  - Introduced `smile.feature.selection.EnsembleSelection` to easily score, rank, and threshold feature importance from Random Forests, Gradient Boosted Trees, and Decision Trees.
- **Java 25 Spark Module**:
  - Modernized `spark` module rewritten in pure Java 25.

### 🔌 Extensibility & Marketplace
- **Claude Code-Style Plugin Marketplace**:
  - Integrated plugin marketplace dialog in Studio, seeded with official plugin catalogs and discovery tools.
- **Scoped MCP Integration**:
  - Support for Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers with per-agent scoping via `x-smile-agents` and automatic omission of redundant provider tools via `x-smile-provides`.

